  "explanation": {
    "md_es": "**Presente simple** = hábitos y rutinas.\n\n- **I / you / we / they** → verbo base: *I work, they work*.\n- **he / she / it** → verbo + **-s**: *she works, he gets up*.\n\n| Terminación del verbo | Cambio | Ejemplo |\n|---|---|---|\n| normal | + s | works, gets |\n| -s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o | + es | finishes, watches, goes |\n| have | has (irregular) | she has |\n\nPronunciación de la -s: /s/ (works), /z/ (gets… *plays*), /ɪz/ (watches, finishes).",
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "She work in a shop.",
        "right": "She works in a shop.",
        "note": "Con he/she/it el verbo lleva -s."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "He haves breakfast.",
        "right": "He has breakfast.",
        "note": "Have es irregular: has."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
